<title>CANADA: No TCK smut in Canadian wheat - CWB official.</title>
<headline>No TCK smut in Canadian wheat - CWB official.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>There is no TCK smut fungus on Canadian-grown wheat despite claims to the contrary made earlier on Monday by a United States Senator, a Canadian Wheat Board official said.</p>
<p>&quot;He, I'm sure, just made an error in including Canada with those other countries because we have been TCK free,&quot; CWB spokeswoman Rhea Yates told Reuters.</p>
<p>U.S. Senator Dirk Kempthorne (R-Idaho), while speaking at a news conference in Washington earlier Monday, said he had complained to Chinese President Jiang Zemin that infected wheat from the United States was banned from China while China imported fungus-tainted wheat from Canada, Germany and France.</p>
<p>The news conference also included other members of a U.S. Senate delegation that had visited China, Vietnam, Hong Kong and Taiwan.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
